# Character policy for the repository. Every grant below is intentional: the
# comment records why a file type needs more than the ASCII floor.
* ascii

# Markdown is specification and project prose. `caveman` covers the notation
# used by the specs; `xenolith-spec-symbols` covers the five set/logic symbols
# that the specs explain and use, declared in .ctrm-sets rather than disabling
# checking with `any`.
*.md ascii+caveman+xenolith-spec-symbols

# Rust source uses the same specification notation and marks as the prose.
*.rs ascii+caveman+marks

# These test modules contain Polish examples; grant the Polish locale only to
# the files that contain those examples rather than widening every Rust file.
src/lint/sites/tests.rs ascii+caveman+marks+pl
src/graph/scan/tests.rs ascii+caveman+marks+pl
languages/shebang/src/tests.rs ascii+caveman+marks+pl
languages/data/xml/tests/lens.rs ascii+caveman+marks+pl
languages/data/xml/src/text/tests.rs ascii+caveman+marks+pl
languages/ci/pkl/tests/lens.rs ascii+caveman+marks+pl
languages/ci/pkl/src/string/tests.rs ascii+caveman+marks+pl
languages/ci/pkl/src/placement/tests.rs ascii+caveman+marks+pl
languages/ci/pkl/src/host/tests.rs ascii+caveman+marks+pl
languages/ci/nix/tests/lens.rs ascii+caveman+marks+pl
languages/ci/nix/src/unescape/tests.rs ascii+caveman+marks+pl
languages/ci/nix/src/placement/tests.rs ascii+caveman+marks+pl
languages/ci/nix/src/bound/tests.rs ascii+caveman+marks+pl
languages/api/src/tests.rs ascii+caveman+marks+pl

*.c ascii+legal
*.txt ascii+legal+caveman
*.pkl ascii+box+caveman
*.bats ascii+caveman
*.nix ascii+caveman
*.plist ascii+caveman
*.sh ascii+caveman
*.toml ascii+caveman
.context-limits ascii+caveman
